257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Topic words are the key terms that indicate the main subject or focus of the question. These words help you to identify what the essay should be about and to guide your research and writing. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
258 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (For example, in a question like "Discuss the significance of the resurrection in Christian theology," the topic words are "significance," "resurrection," and "Christian theology." )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
259 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (Another example could be "Analyze the role of the Holy Spirit in the early church," where the topic words are "role," "Holy Spirit," and "early church." )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
